  "final_response": "Perfect! The changes are ready. Here's a summary of what I've fixed:\n\n## Changes Made:\n\n1. **src/builtin.c (line 645)**: Updated the `@uri` format implementation to follow RFC 3986\n   - Changed unreserved characters from `CHARS_ALPHANUM \"-_.!~*'()\"` to `CHARS_ALPHANUM \"-_.~\"`\n   - This ensures only the characters defined by RFC 3986 are left unencoded: alphanumeric, hyphen, period, underscore, and tilde\n\n2. **tests/jq.test (line 71)**: Updated the expected output for the @uri test\n   - Changed from `\"%3C%3E%26'%22%09\"` to `\"%3C%3E%26%27%22%09\"`\n   - The single quote is now correctly encoded as `%27` instead of appearing as a raw character\n\nThe fix ensures that characters like `!`, `'`, `(`, `)`, and `*` are now percent-encoded as required by RFC 3986, which obsoleted RFC 2396. The implementation is ready to be committed."
